1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,235
Here's a puzzle from this week's code.

2
00:00:02,555 --> 00:00:05,365
Setup crashes with an attribute error:

3
00:00:05,365 --> 00:00:09,211
scGenModel has no attribute x_dimensions,
with an s.

4
00:00:09,367 --> 00:00:14,299
The fix looks like one letter.
Delete the s, and the crash disappears.

5
00:00:14,299 --> 00:00:17,117
We tried it on toy data with four genes,

6
00:00:17,117 --> 00:00:20,780
and a stand-in for scgen:
setup runs, no complaints.

7
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:24,432
But the network would be built
for one thousand genes, not four.

8
00:00:24,752 --> 00:00:27,034
The error is gone, and the bug is not.

9
00:00:27,354 --> 00:00:30,341
To see why, follow one name through five places.

10
00:00:33,667 --> 00:00:37,038
First, the setup you watched Josh work in:
three windows.

11
00:00:37,358 --> 00:00:42,648
The package file, the config file,
and the e24_replica notebook that runs them.

12
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,499
Two wires connect them.

13
00:00:44,549 --> 00:00:47,841
The editable install, the dash e in pip install,

14
00:00:47,841 --> 00:00:51,888
means Python imports your folder itself,
not a frozen copy.

15
00:00:52,208 --> 00:00:57,136
And autoreload, at the top of the notebook,
re-reads the file whenever it changes.

16
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,661
The config wire is even simpler.

17
00:00:59,661 --> 00:01:05,492
Every new Experiment opens config.yaml
and reads it fresh, with yaml.safe_load.

18
00:01:05,734 --> 00:01:09,553
So the loop is: edit a file,
rerun the cell, read what breaks.

19
00:01:09,873 --> 00:01:11,963
That loop is what you watched Josh do.

20
00:01:15,767 --> 00:01:19,692
Now follow one value:
the latent size, z_dimension, fifty.

21
00:01:20,012 --> 00:01:25,580
Hop one: it's a line in config.yaml,
under models, under scGenModel.

22
00:01:25,734 --> 00:01:30,603
Hop two: safe load turns the whole file
into nested Python dictionaries.

23
00:01:30,603 --> 00:01:35,675
A dictionary is a row of labelled drawers.
You open one by its exact label.

24
00:01:35,834 --> 00:01:39,328
Hop three: the experiment's setup, at line 115,

25
00:01:39,328 --> 00:01:45,946
hands the scGenModel drawer to the class,
and init opens the drawer labelled z_dimension.

26
00:01:46,266 --> 00:01:51,108
Hop four: init writes the value onto the object,
as self.z_dimension.

27
00:01:51,267 --> 00:01:53,814
Fifth, the model's own setup method,

28
00:01:53,814 --> 00:01:57,705
at line 254,
reads that attribute to build the network.

29
00:01:57,705 --> 00:02:02,814
Careful there: the name left of the equals sign
is scgen's own parameter.

30
00:02:02,814 --> 00:02:08,972
Ours is the one after self dot. Five places,
and the spelling has to match at every one.

31
00:02:08,972 --> 00:02:11,982
That's why Josh kept jumping between files.

32
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,597
That path has two kinds of lookup,
and each one fails with its own error.

33
00:02:21,597 --> 00:02:25,060
Opening a drawer
that doesn't exist raises a key error.

34
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:29,971
Asking an object for an attribute it never
received raises an attribute error.

35
00:02:30,133 --> 00:02:31,400
Pause and predict:

36
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:35,061
Josh's toy config spells it x_dimensions,
with an s.

37
00:02:35,381 --> 00:02:38,261
Will init raise a key error,
or an attribute error?

38
00:02:42,433 --> 00:02:46,705
A key error.
Build scGenModel from the toy config,

39
00:02:46,705 --> 00:02:49,012
and init stops at line 220:

40
00:02:49,012 --> 00:02:51,692
key error, x_dimension, singular.

41
00:02:52,012 --> 00:02:53,812
The drawer it asked for isn't there.

42
00:02:53,933 --> 00:02:57,533
And the attribute error
is our crash at line 253:

43
00:02:57,533 --> 00:03:03,704
the model's setup asks for self.x_dimensions,
but init only ever wrote the singular.

44
00:03:03,867 --> 00:03:06,171
To read a traceback, start at the bottom.

45
00:03:06,491 --> 00:03:10,368
The last line says what went wrong,
and here Python even asks:

46
00:03:10,368 --> 00:03:12,168
did you mean x_dimension?

47
00:03:12,251 --> 00:03:15,003
Just above it,
the last file and line says where.

48
00:03:15,323 --> 00:03:20,075
Read further up and you see the path:
the experiment's setup,

49
00:03:20,075 --> 00:03:24,048
at line 119,
called the model's setup, at line 253.

50
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:27,974
One caution:
we measured this with a stand-in for scgen.

51
00:03:27,974 --> 00:03:31,727
On the cluster,
a different scgen error can come first.

52
00:03:31,727 --> 00:03:33,527
Episode four explains why.

53
00:03:39,867 --> 00:03:41,545
Now the silent part.

54
00:03:41,595 --> 00:03:43,260
When use_all_genes is true,

55
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:48,316
the experiment's setup is meant to replace
the typed gene count with the real one,

56
00:03:48,316 --> 00:03:49,758
read from the data.

57
00:03:49,808 --> 00:03:51,664
Line 104 does that.

58
00:03:51,834 --> 00:03:55,269
But line 104 writes x_dimensions, with an s.

59
00:03:55,589 --> 00:03:58,907
Writing to a label
that doesn't exist never complains:

60
00:03:58,907 --> 00:04:00,751
Python just adds a new drawer.

61
00:04:01,071 --> 00:04:06,473
So the dictionary ends up with two drawers:
x_dimension, singular, one thousand,

62
00:04:06,473 --> 00:04:10,458
typed by hand, and x_dimensions,
with an s, the real count.

63
00:04:10,634 --> 00:04:12,965
Init only opens the singular drawer,

64
00:04:12,965 --> 00:04:16,138
so the real count lands
in a drawer nobody reads.

65
00:04:16,458 --> 00:04:20,206
On Josh's real data,
his notebook once printed that drawer:

66
00:04:20,206 --> 00:04:22,367
eighteen thousand and twenty-four.

67
00:04:22,687 --> 00:04:24,799
With today's init, nothing reads it.

68
00:04:24,967 --> 00:04:28,810
Pause on this: should the gene count
be typed into the config at all,

69
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:30,983
or should it always come from the data?

70
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:42,801
Four rules turn this back-and-forth
into a routine.

71
00:04:42,967 --> 00:04:46,126
One: one spelling.
The config key, the init line,

72
00:04:46,126 --> 00:04:48,769
and the attribute share exactly one name.

73
00:04:48,769 --> 00:04:50,810
Two: derived values are derived.

74
00:04:50,810 --> 00:04:54,508
A number the data can tell
you shouldn't be typed by hand.

75
00:04:54,667 --> 00:04:56,324
Three: fail early.

76
00:04:56,374 --> 00:05:00,022
Init already reads every key
the moment the object is built.

77
00:05:00,342 --> 00:05:04,779
That's good: a missing key explodes inside init,
not an hour into training.

78
00:05:04,933 --> 00:05:06,449
Four: after any rename,

79
00:05:06,449 --> 00:05:10,603
search the whole project for the old name,
YAML files included.

80
00:05:10,603 --> 00:05:13,275
Then rerun the smallest example you have.

81
00:05:13,433 --> 00:05:17,359
Two traps to check today.
Josh's toy config has drifted:

82
00:05:17,359 --> 00:05:19,391
it has no experiment section,

83
00:05:19,391 --> 00:05:21,215
so setup stops at line 86,

84
00:05:21,215 --> 00:05:25,004
and it also lacks z_dimension,
alpha and dropout rate.

85
00:05:25,004 --> 00:05:30,754
And in YAML, None is just the word None,
a string. YAML spells an empty value null.

86
00:05:30,754 --> 00:05:32,300
That's harmless today,

87
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:35,812
but any check for None
would quietly get it wrong.

88
00:05:40,833 --> 00:05:44,732
Recap.
A config value passes through five places:

89
00:05:44,732 --> 00:05:50,220
a YAML line, a dictionary drawer, init,
an attribute, and the setup that reads it.

90
00:05:50,540 --> 00:05:52,502
Every place needs the same spelling.

91
00:05:52,666 --> 00:05:55,126
A key error means a drawer is missing.

92
00:05:55,126 --> 00:05:59,075
An attribute error means the object never got
that attribute.

93
00:05:59,075 --> 00:06:02,053
And a quiet bug can hide behind a fixed crash.

94
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:05,554
Your exercise:
search the project for both spellings,

95
00:06:05,554 --> 00:06:07,768
and keep the singular, x_dimension.

96
00:06:08,088 --> 00:06:13,805
It already matches config.yaml and init,
and it's the name of scgen's own parameter.

97
00:06:14,125 --> 00:06:18,483
Change line 104,
the right-hand side of line 253,

98
00:06:18,483 --> 00:06:20,973
and the toy config to match.

99
00:06:21,293 --> 00:06:23,241
Then rerun e24_replica,

100
00:06:23,241 --> 00:06:28,828
and check that the model's
x_dimension is now the real gene count,

101
00:06:28,828 --> 00:06:32,045
even if setup still stops at line 252.

102
00:06:32,365 --> 00:06:34,541
Episode four explains that stop.
